1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-1--1a-the-absolute-basics","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-1/1a-the-absolute-basics","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-1/1a-the-absolute-basics","sourceHash":"da42099592088fed87cbad5dc1aa777a0887e4c9b08682153a7b4b70bdf0219a","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:37.887Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"1A — The Absolute Basics","zh":"1A — 绝对基础"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你要做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"All language learning journeys start at the beginning — with no (or almost no) knowledge of the target language. This sub-phase is about getting your bearings. Before you can make big plans or learn much of anything, you need to understand the most basic sounds, see how sentences are put together, and pick up a handful of core words.","zh":"所有语言学习之旅都从起点开始——对目标语言一无所知或几乎一无所知。这个子阶段的重点是了解基本情况。在制定宏大计划或学习大量内容之前，你需要理解最基础的发音，看看句子是如何组织的，并掌握一些核心词汇。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Think of it like getting dropped into the middle of a foreign city without a map and trying to find your way around. If you ever want to get out of there you first need to orient yourself so you don't just walk in circles.","zh":"想象一下，你被丢进一座陌生城市的中心，手里没有地图，还要设法找到方向。如果你想离开那里，首先必须确定自己的方位，否则只会一直兜圈子。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Since this is the very first sub-phase, everything is new. You'll be doing two kinds of learning from the start: <strong>priming</strong> and <strong>immersion</strong>. These are the pillars of the entire method — if you neglect one, your routine will be structurally weak and you won't make the progress you want. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"由于这是第一个子阶段，一切都是新的。从一开始，你会进行两类学习：<strong>预热</strong>和<strong>沉浸</strong>。它们是整个方法的支柱——忽视任何一项，你的学习安排都会缺少结构，也无法取得理想的进步。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"priming-activities","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Priming Activities","zh":"预热活动"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming means learning <em>about</em> the language so that you're more prepared to understand it during immersion. There are several kinds of priming you'll do in this sub-phase:","zh":"预热是指学习<em>关于</em>这门语言的知识，从而为在沉浸过程中理解它做好更充分的准备。在这个子阶段，你会进行几种预热活动："}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Vocab Study</strong> — You need to know words before you can understand anything. You'll use a spaced repetition system (SRS) to efficiently learn your first 100 words. We recommend Anki, which is free, cross-platform, and backed by an excellent review algorithm. Starting with a pre-made deck of common words is the fastest way to get going. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/learning-words-with-anki\">Learning Words with Anki</a>","zh":"<strong>词汇学习</strong>——在理解任何内容之前，你需要先认识其中的单词。你将使用间隔重复系统（SRS）高效学习最初的 100 个单词。我们推荐 Anki，它免费、跨平台，并采用优秀的复习算法。使用包含常用词的预制牌组，是最快的入门方式。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/learning-words-with-anki\">使用 Anki 学习单词</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Sound Study</strong> — Each language uses a set of sounds that are almost certainly different from your native language. Learning about these sounds early prepares your ears to notice them during immersion, even if you can't perfectly hear them yet. YouTube is a great place to find guides on the sound system (phonology) of most languages. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/sound-study\">Sound Study</a>","zh":"<strong>发音学习</strong>——每种语言都有一套发音，而这些发音几乎肯定不同于你的母语。尽早了解这些发音，可以让你的耳朵在沉浸过程中更容易注意到它们，即使你还无法完美地听辨出来。YouTube 是查找大多数语言发音系统（音系学）指南的好地方。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/sound-study\">发音学习</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Grammar Study</strong> — This is not traditional grammar study. You won't be doing drills or memorizing conjugation tables. Grammar priming is comprehension-focused: you're learning just enough about how sentences work to help you understand what you hear and read. Free YouTube courses exist for most languages. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/grammar-priming\">Grammar Priming</a>","zh":"<strong>语法学习</strong>——这不是传统意义上的语法学习。你不会做练习题，也不会背诵动词变位表。语法预热以理解为导向：你只需学习足够理解句子运作方式的内容，帮助自己理解听到和读到的内容。大多数语言都有免费的 YouTube 课程。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/grammar-priming\">语法预热</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Writing System Study</strong> — You need to be able to read in your target language to effectively use learning tools. Some writing systems are very close to English (Spanish, French) and can be learned in an hour. Others (Arabic, Korean) take much longer. If your language uses a character system like Chinese or Japanese, start with the phonetic system (pinyin, kana) — don't dive into characters yet. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/writing-system-study\">Writing System Study</a>","zh":"<strong>文字系统学习</strong>——要有效使用学习工具，你需要能够阅读目标语言。有些文字系统与英语非常接近（西班牙语、法语），一小时就能学会。另一些（阿拉伯语、韩语）则需要更长时间。如果你的语言使用中文或日语那样的字符系统，请先从语音系统开始（拼音、假名），暂时不要钻研汉字或日文汉字。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/writing-system-study\">文字系统学习</a>"}},{"id":"immersion-activities","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Immersion Activities","zh":"沉浸活动"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming on its own won't get you anywhere if you don't actually spend time with the language. This is the main reason traditional language teaching fails — it skips the most important part: real time with the language.","zh":"如果你不真正花时间接触这门语言，单靠预热不会让你走得更远。这也是传统语言教学失败的主要原因——它跳过了最重要的部分：真正与语言相处的时间。"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>The Noticing Game</strong> — The simplest immersion activity you can do. Instead of trying to understand everything (which is impossible right now), you shift your focus to <em>noticing</em>. Notice words you learned in Anki, sounds you studied, patterns that repeat. Anything counts. This trains your brain to pay attention to the language even when most of it is still gibberish. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-noticing-game\">The Noticing Game</a>","zh":"<strong>注意力游戏</strong>——这是你能进行的最简单的沉浸活动。此时想要理解所有内容是不可能的，因此不要试图全部理解，而是把注意力转向<em>留意</em>。留意你在 Anki 中学过的单词、学过的发音，以及反复出现的规律。任何发现都算数。即使大部分内容听起来仍像一团乱码，这也能训练大脑关注这门语言。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-noticing-game\">注意力游戏</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"To play the Noticing Game, you'll need content in your target language. As a total beginner, two kinds work best:","zh":"要玩注意力游戏，你需要目标语言内容。作为完全初学者，以下两类内容最适合："}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Comprehensible Input</strong> — Native speakers who make videos specifically for learners, using simplified language with lots of visual context so you can guess meaning. These are widely available on YouTube for most languages. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/comprehensible-input\">Comprehensible Input</a>","zh":"<strong>可理解输入</strong>——母语者专门为学习者制作视频，使用简化语言并提供大量视觉语境，让你可以猜测意思。大多数语言都能在 YouTube 上找到这类内容。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/comprehensible-input\">可理解输入</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Beginner-Level Content</strong> — Things that are inherently simple, like children's TV shows or simplified stories. These aren't made for learners, but they're easy enough to start with. Shows dubbed into your target language that you already know (like a childhood favorite) can be especially powerful because you already understand the story. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/beginner-level-content\">Beginner-Level Content</a>","zh":"<strong>初学者级内容</strong>——内容本身就很简单，例如儿童电视节目或简化故事。这些内容并非为学习者制作，但足够简单，适合入门。将你已经熟悉的节目（例如童年时喜欢的作品）配上目标语言配音尤其有效，因为你已经理解故事情节。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/beginner-level-content\">初学者级内容</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的学习安排"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"During this sub-phase, aim for this split:","zh":"在这个子阶段，目标是按以下比例安排时间："}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>50%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>互动沉浸：</strong>50%"}]},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"30 minutes of each (1 hour total per day) is an excellent goal. 15 minutes of each is the minimum — lower than that and you won't feel any progress.","zh":"每项 30 分钟（每天共 1 小时）是很好的目标。每项 15 分钟是最低标准——再少的话，你会感觉不到进步。"}},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0023","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Anki vocabulary study: 15-20 mins","zh":"使用 Anki 学习词汇：15–20 分钟"},{"en":"Basic grammar concepts: 5-10 mins","zh":"基础语法概念：5–10 分钟"},{"en":"Sound system practice: 5-10 mins","zh":"发音系统练习：5–10 分钟"},{"en":"Comprehensible input with noticing: 30 mins","zh":"结合留意练习可理解输入：30 分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0025","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 1B when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入 1B："}},{"id":"segment-0026","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Have learned 100 words","zh":"已经学会 100 个单词"},{"en":"Have tried each of the activities in this sub-phase","zh":"已经尝试过这个子阶段中的每项活动"},{"en":"Are comfortable with a daily learning routine","zh":"已经适应每日学习安排"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0028","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The two-pillar approach of priming and immersion is grounded in Krashen's Acquisition-Learning Distinction (1982), which established that language knowledge comes from two sources: acquisition (implicit, picked up from exposure) and study (explicit, conscious learning). Neither alone is sufficient — this is why the roadmap pairs grammar priming and vocabulary study with actual immersion time in real content.","zh":"预热与沉浸的双支柱方法建立在 Krashen 的《习得—学习区别》（1982）之上。该理论认为，语言知识来自两个来源：习得（通过接触隐性获得）和学习（有意识地进行显性学习）。单独依靠任何一项都不够——因此，路线图将语法预热和词汇学习与真实内容中的实际沉浸时间结合起来。"}},{"id":"segment-0029","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Spaced repetition systems like Anki are backed by strong research: Nakata (2015) found that spaced repetition significantly outperforms massed practice for vocabulary retention, while Serfaty (2023) confirmed that spaced relearning is critical for long-term retention. The brain needs repeated exposure at strategic intervals to move vocabulary from short-term to long-term memory.","zh":"Anki 这样的间隔重复系统有充分的研究支持：Nakata（2015）发现，间隔重复在词汇保持方面明显优于集中练习；Serfaty（2023）则确认，间隔式再学习对长期记忆至关重要。大脑需要在经过策略安排的间隔中反复接触词汇，才能将其从短期记忆转移到长期记忆。"}},{"id":"segment-0030","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The emphasis on noticing (through the Noticing Game and comprehensible input) draws from Schmidt's Noticing Hypothesis (1990), which argues that learners cannot acquire a language feature they haven't consciously noticed. While you can't understand everything as a beginner, deliberately noticing patterns you do recognize primes your brain to acquire more complex structures during immersion.","zh":"对留意的重视（通过注意力游戏和可理解输入）源于 Schmidt 的注意假说（1990）。该假说认为，学习者无法习得自己没有有意识注意到的语言特征。作为初学者，你不可能理解所有内容，但有意识地留意自己能识别的规律，可以为大脑在沉浸过程中习得更复杂的结构做好准备。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
